THIS IS ONLY IF MANUAL BACKUP IS THE OPTION.  OTHERWISE, USE THE SCRIPT backup.sh TO BACKUP

# CCDC Linux Backup Commands

## Setup

```bash
sudo -i
BACKUP_DIR="/var/tmp/ccdc_backup_$(date +%Y%m%d_%H%M%S)"
mkdir -m 700 "$BACKUP_DIR"
cd "$BACKUP_DIR"
umask 077
```

## 1. System Configurations

```bash
tar --acls --xattrs --selinux -cpf etc.tar /etc
```

## 2. Databases

### MySQL
```bash
mysqldump -u root -p --all-databases --single-transaction --routines --events --triggers > mysql.sql
```

### MariaDB
```bash
mariadb-dump -u root -p --all-databases --single-transaction --routines --events --triggers > mariadb.sql
```

### PostgreSQL
```bash
sudo -u postgres pg_dumpall > postgres.sql
```

## 3. Website and Application Files

```bash
tar -cpf www.tar /var/www
tar -cpf opt.tar /opt
tar -cpf srv.tar /srv
```

Only back up directories that exist.

## 4. Users, Passwords and Groups

```bash
tar -cpf users.tar /etc/passwd /etc/shadow /etc/group /etc/gshadow
```

## 5. SSH Configuration

```bash
tar -cpf ssh.tar /etc/ssh
```

## 6. Cron Jobs

```bash
tar -cpf cron.tar /var/spool/cron /etc/cron*
```

## 7. Firewall

### Firewalld
```bash
tar -cpf firewall.tar /etc/firewalld
```

### iptables
```bash
iptables-save > iptables.rules
```

## 8. Systemd Services and Timers

```bash
tar -cpf systemd.tar /etc/systemd/system
```

## 9. Home Directories and SSH Keys

```bash
tar --acls --xattrs --selinux --exclude='home/rocky/recovery' -cpf home.tar -C / home root
```

## 10. Sudo Permissions

```bash
tar -cpf sudo.tar /etc/sudoers /etc/sudoers.d
```

## Secure Backup Files

```bash
chown root:rocky .
chmod 750 .
find . -maxdepth 1 -type f -exec chown root:rocky {} \;
find . -maxdepth 1 -type f -exec chmod 640 {} \;
find . -maxdepth 1 -type f -exec chattr +i {} \;
```

